{'id':'Q01','source_passages':[{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle','quotation':'**Rule (2.5):** A player rules a clearing with more total **warriors plus buildings** than each other player. Tokens and pawns do not contribute. Ordinary ties mean nobody rules. Eyrie rule a tie for most if they have at least one Eyrie piece there. Vagabond cannot rule or stop someone else ruling.'}],'answer':[{'part':'Determining rule','ruling':'Compare each player’s total warriors plus buildings in the clearing; a player rules only when their total is greater than every other player’s total.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Rule 2.5)'},{'part':'Ordinary tie','ruling':'An ordinary tie for most means nobody rules the clearing.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Rule 2.5)'},{'part':'Eyrie tie','ruling':'The Eyrie rule a tie for most if they have at least one Eyrie piece in that clearing.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Rule 2.5)'},{'part':'Tokens and Vagabond pawn','ruling':'Tokens and pawns do not contribute to rule. The Vagabond cannot rule a clearing and cannot stop another player from ruling it.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Rule 2.5)'}],'support':'supported','evidence':['Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Rule 2.5)']},
{'id':'Q02','source_passages':[{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle','quotation':'**Move (4.2):** Take any positive number of your warriors/pawns from one clearing along a linking path to an adjacent clearing. You must rule origin or destination or both. Recheck rule for each move. You may move the same pieces repeatedly, including on multiple moves in one action. Rivers are not paths unless an effect explicitly treats them as paths.'}],'answer':[{'part':'Legality of a normal move','ruling':'Move a positive number of your own warriors or pawns from one clearing along a linking path to an adjacent clearing, and rule the origin, destination, or both. Recheck rule for each move.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Move 4.2)'},{'part':'Repeated movement','ruling':'The same pieces may move repeatedly, including in multiple moves within one action.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Move 4.2)'},{'part':'Rivers','ruling':'Rivers do not count as paths unless an effect explicitly treats them as paths.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Move 4.2)'}],'support':'supported','evidence':['Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Move 4.2)']},
{'id':'Q03','source_passages':[{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle','quotation':'**Battle (4.3):** Choose a clearing with your warriors or pawn and an enemy there as defender. **Battle does not require you to rule the clearing.** Resolve these six steps:'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Battle','quotation':'1. **Ambush:** Defender may play one ambush matching clearing (birds are wild). Attacker may foil it with a matching ambush. Defender\'s card is discarded; a foiled ambush deals no hits. Otherwise defender immediately deals two hits, then discards ambush. If no attacking warriors or pawns remain, battle ends immediately. Ambush hits are not limited by defending warriors.'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Battle','quotation':'3. **Roll:** Higher die is attacker\'s rolled hits, lower defender\'s; equal dice give equal results. Each side\'s rolled hits are capped by its own warriors in battle. Alliance defending reverses the dice; Vagabond uses undamaged swords instead of warriors.'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Battle','quotation':'5. **Count hits:** Add extra hits (uncapped by warriors), subtract ignored hits. If defender has no warriors, attacker deals one extra hit for **defenseless**; Vagabond is instead defenseless if it has no undamaged swords.'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Battle','quotation':'6. **Deal hits:** Each hit removes one opposing piece. The side taking hits chooses its own removal order, but **all its warriors must be removed before its buildings/tokens**. It also chooses order of effects triggered by its pieces\' removal. Both sides deal their counted hits; losing warriors does not retroactively change the rolled cap. Whoever removes an enemy building/token scores **one VP each**, even while defending and even outside battle. Vagabond takes hits as item damage instead.'}],'answer':[{'part':'Battle setup and ambush','ruling':'To initiate battle, choose a clearing containing your warriors or pawn and an enemy defender; you need not rule it. The defender may play one matching ambush (birds are wild). The attacker may foil with a matching ambush; the defender’s card is discarded and a foiled ambush causes no hits. Otherwise the defender immediately deals two hits and discards the ambush. If no attacking warriors or pawns remain after those hits, battle ends immediately; ambush hits are not capped by defending warriors.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Battle 4.3, steps 1)'},{'part':'Dice and hit limits','ruling':'The higher die is the attacker’s rolled hits and the lower die the defender’s; equal dice give both equal results. Each side caps its rolled hits by its own warriors in battle. When Alliance defends, it reverses the dice assignment. Vagabond uses undamaged swords instead of warriors for its rolled-hit limit.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Battle 4.3, step 3)'},{'part':'Count hits','ruling':'Add extra hits without a warrior cap, then subtract ignored hits. If the defender has no warriors, the attacker gets one defenseless hit; Vagabond is defenseless instead when it has no undamaged swords.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Battle 4.3, step 5)'},{'part':'Deal hits, removal priorities, and VP','ruling':'Each hit removes one opposing piece. The side taking hits chooses its removal order, but must remove all its warriors before its buildings or tokens; it also orders effects triggered by its pieces’ removal. Both sides deal their counted hits, and losing warriors does not retroactively change rolled-hit caps. Whoever removes an enemy building or token scores one VP for each, including while defending or outside battle. Vagabond takes hits as item damage.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Battle 4.3, step 6)'}],'support':'supported','evidence':['Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Battle 4.3)']},
{'id':'Q04','source_passages':[{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Craft','quotation':'**Craft (4.1):** **Every crafting piece gets its suit from the clearing containing it.** The card\'s **bottom-left crafting icons** require pieces of those clearing suits; the card\'s own suit does not define the cost. Craft a card from hand when your faction permits.'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Craft','quotation':'- **Marquise, Eyrie and Alliance cost:** For **each icon**, activate **one workshop, roost or sympathy in a clearing matching that icon\'s suit**, respectively. A crafting piece gets its suit from its clearing. Combine eligible pieces as needed, but **each piece may activate only once per turn**.'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Craft','quotation':'- Immediate effect (paper box): resolve, then discard the **crafting card**. An item card requires the corresponding **item token** in the map supply, or it cannot be crafted. Take the item token into Crafted Items and score the VP printed on the card, subject to Eyrie exception. The item token stays; the crafting card is discarded. Ordinary factions do not exhaust crafted items as Vagabond does.'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Craft','quotation':'- Persistent effect (stone box): keep card in your play area and gain its text, subject to the personal duplicate check above. Its card is outside your hand and cannot be spent/discarded/used for another purpose unless explicitly instructed.'},{'section':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle — Craft','quotation':'**Personal duplicate check:** Only an identical persistent effect **in your own play area** prevents you from crafting that effect again. Other players\' copies do not count for this duplicate restriction.'}],'answer':[{'part':'Crafting cost and piece suits','ruling':'Craft a card from hand when permitted by your faction, paying its bottom-left icons with crafting pieces whose clearing suits match each icon; the card’s own suit does not set the cost. Marquise activates workshops, Eyrie roosts, and Alliance sympathy, one eligible piece per icon.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Craft 4.1)'},{'part':'Repeat use of pieces','ruling':'Marquise, Eyrie, and Alliance each may activate a crafting piece only once per turn.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Craft 4.1, Marquise/Eyrie/Alliance cost)'},{'part':'Unavailable item supply','ruling':'An item card cannot be crafted if its corresponding item token is absent from the map supply.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Craft, immediate effect)'},{'part':'Duplicate persistent effects','ruling':'Only an identical persistent effect already in your own play area prevents crafting it again; another player’s copy does not trigger this restriction.','evidence':'Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Personal duplicate check)'}],'support':'supported','evidence':['Actions — Shared movement, crafting and battle (Craft 4.1; Personal duplicate check)']},
{'id':'Q05','source_passages':[{'section':'Scoring / Victory Conditions — Dominance','quotation':'**Dominance (3.3):** In own Daylight at **at least 10 VP**, activate a dominance card from hand into play area; remove score marker and stop scoring VP. Cannot remove/replace activated card. At **start of own Birdsong**, win if ruling **three clearings of matching mouse/rabbit/fox suit**, or for **bird dominance, two diagonally opposite corner clearings**. Meeting condition earlier does not immediately win. Dominance cards cannot be crafted, but can be spent for suit. Whenever one would enter discard, put it near map available instead. During own Daylight, spend matching card to take available dominance into hand. Available **bird dominance remains bird**, so payment must be bird; a bird hand card can pay for non-bird dominance. Activation and taking are separate, neither requires a faction action allowance.'}],'answer':[{'part':'Activation timing and threshold','ruling':'During your own Daylight, at 10 or more VP, activate a dominance card from hand into your play area; remove your score marker and stop scoring VP.','evidence':'Scoring / Victory Conditions — Dominance (3.3)'},{'part':'Victory conditions by suit','ruling':'At the start of your own Birdsong, mouse, rabbit, or fox dominance wins if you rule three clearings of the matching suit. Bird dominance wins if you rule two diagonally opposite corner clearings. Meeting a condition before that timing does not immediately win.','evidence':'Scoring / Victory Conditions — Dominance (3.3)'},{'part':'Activated card disposition','ruling':'An activated dominance card cannot be removed or replaced.','evidence':'Scoring / Victory Conditions — Dominance (3.3)'}],'support':'supported','evidence':['Scoring / Victory Conditions — Dominance (3.3)']}
]
# Separate coverage audit: all requested subclauses have a labeled application; citations are checked independently below.
required={'Q01':4,'Q02':3,'Q03':4,'Q04':4,'Q05':3}
for a in answers:
